WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.000
In a tight corridor, a plausible centerline still leaves little room for the vehicle.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:12.000
A small lateral shift can turn clearance into overlap. The vehicle footprint matters.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:18.000
A small forward shift changes where the vehicle meets crossing traffic.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:25.000
DriveTTO starts with endpoint requests, completed through a native parent trajectory.

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:33.000
Score the complete path. Store its utility at the endpoint that the path actually reaches.

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:43.000
Nearby achieved states guide the next requests toward a promising region.

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:51.000
The archive uses eight neighbors in position, heading and speed. This view projects XY.

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:58.000
Each new request produces another complete path, which is evaluated before updating the archive.

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:07.000
The accepted endpoint plan and a second planner provide different complete motions.

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:17.000
Bounded interpolation and geometric refinement establish one shared trajectory center.

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:28.000
Small longitudinal, lateral and timing changes refine the path around this center.

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:38.000
Proposals from both frozen planners contribute alternative local shapes.

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:48.000
A control branch transfers a bounded change between two rollouts onto the same center.

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:56.000
Zero control perturbation preserves the center. Both branches retain a complete trajectory.

00:01:56.000 --> 00:02:05.000
Proposal and control outputs are combined at matching future timestamps.

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:14.000
Smooth temporal weights allow the early and late parts to use different branch contributions.

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:22.000
Compare each complete candidate with its reference. Configured dual-scoring stages use both heads.

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:31.000
An admitted update replaces the reference; otherwise the reference is kept exactly.

00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:40.000
Endpoint search finds promising motions; local refinement adjusts their geometry and timing.

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:48.000
The same complete motion links the endpoint, the narrow passage and the crossing interaction.
